# Force LF line endings for all shell scripts (cross-platform)
*.sh text eol=lf
# Markdown and JSON are safe with LF too
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
# The JS entry point must be LF too. It is the npm `bin` target, so on
# macOS/Linux npm runs it through its shebang line — and a CRLF file leaves a
# stray carriage return after "node", which makes env fail with
# "No such file or directory". Missed by the v2.10.2 CRLF pass; caught 2026-07-30.
*.js text eol=lf
# The framework's own state files have no extension, so the rules above never
# matched them. A CRLF manifest puts a stray CR into every recorded digest and
# breaks skill comparison exactly as a CRLF SKILL.md does.
.cc-discipline-version text eol=lf
.cc-discipline-skills.manifest text eol=lf
# .gitignore has no extension either, so the rules above never matched it. This
# project has been bitten by CRLF four times; do not leave another file uncovered.
.gitignore text eol=lf
